AI Moderation and Trust & Safety Policy (Draft v1.0)
Purpose

The purpose of the AI Moderation and Trust & Safety System is to promote a safe, respectful, and age-appropriate environment for all participants while preserving privacy, creativity, expression, and community engagement.

The platform uses a combination of automated safety systems, human moderation, user reporting tools, and age-based environment controls.

AI moderation is designed to assist human moderators, not replace them.

Core Principles
Safety First

The protection of users, particularly minors, is a primary platform objective.

Human Oversight

No permanent account action shall be based solely on automated moderation without the opportunity for human review.

Privacy by Design

Moderation systems shall operate using the minimum information necessary to enforce platform rules and maintain community safety.

Transparency

Users shall be informed that communications and platform activities may be analysed by automated safety systems for the purposes of:

Abuse prevention
Community moderation
Fraud prevention
Account security
Trust and safety investigations
Fairness

Moderation decisions shall be applied consistently regardless of:

Age
Gender
Ethnicity
Religion
Nationality
Political beliefs
Disability status
Moderation Model

The platform utilizes a three-layer moderation framework.

Layer 1: Automated AI Safety Systems

AI systems continuously monitor platform activity for potential policy violations.

Examples include:

Text chat
Private messages
Voice communications (if enabled)
Usernames
Display names
Profile biographies
Marketplace listings
User-generated content
Avatar content
Housing descriptions
Community group content

The AI system assigns risk scores and safety flags.

The AI does not determine guilt.

The AI identifies content and behaviour requiring review.

Layer 2: User Controls

Users are provided with self-protection tools including:

Block User
Mute User
Ignore User
Leave Area
Restrict Communication
Report User

These tools are available regardless of moderation outcomes.

Layer 3: Human Moderation Team

Human moderators review:

User reports
AI-generated escalations
Appeals
Serious safety incidents

Human moderators may:

Issue warnings
Restrict communications
Suspend accounts
Remove content
Permanently terminate accounts
Escalate incidents to Trust & Safety specialists
Teen Environment Safeguards (13–17)

The Teen Environment operates under enhanced safety controls.

Additional protections include:

Age-restricted access
Enhanced automated monitoring
Increased moderation coverage
Faster report review times
Restricted communication options
Parent and guardian controls (where applicable)
Strict content approval policies

Teen users may not:

Exchange external contact information
Share phone numbers
Share email addresses
Share social media identifiers
Circumvent age restrictions

Attempts to direct users to external platforms may trigger safety review.

Adult Environment Safeguards (18+)

Adult users have broader communication and social freedoms.

However, the following remain prohibited:

Harassment
Threats
Fraud
Impersonation
Hate speech
Non-consensual sexual content
Exploitation
Platform manipulation

Adult communications remain subject to moderation and safety review.

