Risk-Based Escalation Framework
Low Risk

Examples:

Minor profanity
Community disputes
Non-severe rule violations

Actions:

Logging
Automated warning
User reporting options
Medium Risk

Examples:

Repeated harassment
Persistent unwanted contact
Marketplace misconduct

Actions:

Moderator review
Temporary communication restrictions
High Risk

Examples:

Child safety concerns
Threats of violence
Exploitation indicators
Serious fraud attempts

Actions:

Immediate escalation
Content preservation
Account restrictions
Human investigation
Reporting System

Users may report:

Messages
Profiles
Avatars
User-generated content
Marketplace listings
Virtual homes
Communities
Groups
Voice communications

Reports should automatically include:

Account ID
Timestamp
Relevant conversation logs
Room or location information
Available evidence

Reporters may optionally provide additional information.

Account Actions

Platform enforcement actions may include:

Informational
Educational notice
Safety reminder
Corrective
Warning
Content removal
Feature restriction
Restrictive
Temporary mute
Suspension
Marketplace restriction
Permanent
Account termination
Device bans
Associated-account investigation
Appeals Process

Users may appeal moderation decisions.

Appeals shall receive:

Human review
Case reassessment
Evidence evaluation

Successful appeals may result in:

Removed penalties
Restored content
Account reinstatement
Child Safety Escalation

Reports involving potential child exploitation, grooming, or similar serious safety concerns receive priority handling.

Such incidents may be escalated to:

Dedicated Trust & Safety personnel
Child safety specialists
Appropriate authorities where legally required

The platform reserves the right to preserve evidence necessary for investigations.

Moderator Accountability

Moderator actions must be:

Logged
Auditable
Reviewable

Moderators shall not access user information beyond what is required to perform safety, moderation, or investigation duties.

Age Progression Considerations

When a Teen Environment user transitions into the Adult Environment:

The following may transfer:

Username
Eligible inventory
Avatar identity
Housing assets
Purchases

The following shall not automatically transfer:

Friend relationships
Private messages
Teen community memberships
Teen social graphs

This separation protects both privacy and user safety.

Guiding Philosophy

The platform does not attempt to eliminate all risk, which is impossible in any online environment.

Instead, the platform seeks to:

Establish strong age-based boundaries.
Detect harmful behaviour early.
Provide effective user safety tools.
Preserve user privacy.
Support fair moderation.
Protect minors through enhanced safeguards.
Create a safe and welcoming experience for all participants.

AI assists safety efforts. Human judgment remains responsible for significant moderation decisions.
